   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region, and I have not run it through a validator.\n\n**Macrocycle.** The ring is a 12-membered DOTA-type ring with four nitrogens. Three nitrogens carry CH2COOH arms. The fourth carries CH2C(=O)NH\u2013, which links to the glutamic-acid core.\n\n**Core.** The core is a glutamic acid whose \u03b1-NH is acylated by that DOTA arm. Both the \u03b1-carboxyl and the \u03b3-carboxyl are amidated. No wedge is drawn at this carbon, so I gave it no stereo.\n\n**Two identical arms.** Each arm is built as follows:\n- It starts with NH\u2013(CH2)5\u2013C(=O), which is 6-aminohexanoyl. I counted five CH2 groups between the NH and the C=O.\n- That is amide-linked to a 2,3-diaminopropionic acid unit, NH\u2013CH(COOH)\u2013CH2\u2013NH.\n- The terminal NH is acylated by indazole-5-carbonyl.\n- Indazole N1 carries a (CH2)3\u2013NH\u2013 chain ending in a 2-aminoimidazole.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** In the top arm, the wedge on the diaminopropionic \u03b1-carbon points to the CH2. Using priorities N > COOH > CH2 > H, I assigned R, which gives `[C@@H]` in the SMILES as written. The bottom arm has the same wedge pattern but mirrored, which gives S and `[C@H]`.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)NC(CCC(=O)NCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(=O)O)CNC(=O)c2ccc3c(c2)cnn3CCCNc2ncc[nH]2)C(=O)NCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)O)CNC(=O)c2ccc3c(c2)cnn3CCCNc2ncc[nH]2)CC1"
